  {
   "id": "u05-aorist-1",
   "type": "verb",
   "label": "ἔλυσα",
   "sub": "The first aorist",
   "drills": [
    "gloss-mc",
    "gloss-type",
    "form-recognition",
    "parse",
    "supply-form",
    "principal-parts"
   ],
   "rule": {
    "title": "A snapshot, not a movie",
    "body": "Aorist = augment + σα + endings: ἔ-λυ-σα, ἔλυσας, ἔλυσε(ν), ἐλύσαμεν, ἐλύσατε, ἔλυσαν. Where the imperfect films the action in progress, the aorist photographs it whole. It is the ordinary narrative past ('he said, he went, he healed'), but it says nothing about duration. Liquids: ἀπέστειλα, ἔκρινα, ἔμεινα.",
    "examples": [
     {
      "gr": "ἐπίστευσαν εἰς αὐτόν",
      "en": "they believed in him"
     },
     {
      "gr": "ἔσωσεν ἡμᾶς",
      "en": "he saved us"
     },
     {
      "gr": "ἀπέστειλεν ὁ θεὸς τὸν υἱόν",
      "en": "God sent the Son"
     }
    ]
   },
